{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/212169-being-a-wolf-blooded-fractal-your-opinion","id":212169,"title":"Being a wolf-blooded Fractal, your opinion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-28T23:25:50-07:00","id":212169,"title":"Being a wolf-blooded Fractal, your opinion?","content":"Just something that was in my head, I know major templates wipe minor ones, but I've seen nothing on two minor templates and as this is a possible hereditary condition, how do you think it could work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T02:30:34-07:00","id":212259,"title":"","content":"Down that path lays Samuel Haight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T02:46:28-07:00","id":212265,"title":"","content":"I don't see how it breaks anything to impart Mother Moon's double-edged blessing upon a fractal in the right circumstances, provided you have a reason it makes for a good story. I'm not sure if a demon would be able to assume the Wolf-Blooded condition as a Cover, though, so since a fractal has two demon parents, I would think this would be more likely as a case of being touched by Luna in life rather than born with the touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T03:32:40-07:00","id":212289,"title":"","content":"I like where your going. Though speaking via genetics, it's possible to birth a Fractal from two Latents. So long as they both carry the &quot;Hf&quot; gene there is a 25% chance of a fractal being born. So, if say one of the parents is wolf-blooded, it could stand to reason that a child born to them could be both (I don't know exactly how Wolf-blooded works, from what little I read it just means that the family has a blood relation to a werewolf, I'm not sure how it passes along or if there is an actual genetic component to it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","user":"FallenXanderel","date":". 07-29-2014, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T03:54:43-07:00","id":212297,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm sorry for being ignorant, but who Is Samuel Haight? <br /> <br /> Update: I just read the Wiki on him...I get it now. Though w/ the major template rule that it wipes all minor templates from a character, Haight couldn't exist in nWoD, amusing as that might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","user":"FallenXanderel","date":". 07-29-2014, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:04:02-07:00","id":212302,"title":"","content":"Sam Haight was a character in the Classic World of Darkness who served as the antagonist across a couple different adventure modules, over the course of which he kept grafting different parts of supernatural templates onto himself. He'd started as Garou kinfolk, cWoD Werewolf's equivalent of wolf-blooded, and by his final appearance he had become a full werewolf, obtained vampiric powers by drinking vampire blood, and gotten an artifact that granted him the sorcery of a mage (and a powerful one at that). He's a spooky bedtime story told to scare children away from the dangers of getting too ridiculous mixing things from different games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:08:28-07:00","id":212325,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://boardgamegeek.com/geeklist/147814/history-samuel-haight-spoilers\" target=\"_blank\">This fella described here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:22:04-07:00","id":212330,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just did my reading...though shouldn't he have been something close to an abomination or since he was ghouled and not turned was he spared that fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:37:44-07:00","id":212336,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk turned Ghoul from hunting vampires, who eventually gets a tremere and his library, does his research and finds a way to pelt werewolves in order to become one himself, who then steals the avatar of a mage with a legendary sword that is conveniently destroyed at the end of the adventure, who then gets a mighty artifact called Staff of the World Tree, who continues to be a ghoul and therefore has access to even high levels of Thaumaturgy. Finally, he built so much paradox in his mad bid for power at the search of an antedilivian vampire that it explodes and leaves only a smoking skeleton. In the underworld, his remains are an ashtray.<br /> <br /> Then Ethan Skemp resurrected him by popular demand with W20 strench goals, apparently merely as a Garou, in a properly crafted story module. I like to think that's a good way to redeem 20 years of bad writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:46:54-07:00","id":212341,"title":"","content":"Nightmarish <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VillainSue\" target=\"_blank\">Gary Stu</a> of the CWoD. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Samuel_Haight\" target=\"_blank\">Wolfblooded (later werewolf) self-Ghouled Sorcerer/Mage.</a> And yes he was as twinked as he sounds. Currently an ectoplasmic ashtray. Recently got a facelift in the SAS Skinners to be less of a raging paradox given life.<br /> <br /> That said, minor templates can stack without nessicarily getting that bad. For example, pending the new rules in the Idigram Chronicles, I'd lean more towards a Latent or an Offspring Wolfblooded. I'd shy away from Fractal Wolfblooded, because in universe it doesn't make sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:39:59-07:00","id":212549,"title":"","content":"Back on track.<br /> <br /> I've been toying with the idea in my head myself, and I find myself preferring using a mixed lineage as an opportunity for siblings rather than a mix over. That said, if it seems like fun and a fit for your game, a Wolf-blooded Heir is probably almost as powerful as a major template, and that way promises a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T22:01:30-07:00","id":215547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/212169-being-a-wolf-blooded-fractal-your-opinion?p=212259#post212259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Down that path lays Samuel Haight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The path that leads to tears, RAEGE, and suffering for all? Have the prophesies of the dreaded Haight come to pass?<br /> <br /> Less joking note, it does seem to be rather game breaky, especially since wolf blooded now can shape shift or have other strange spiritual abilities. combine that with the inherent power of a Fractal.. why would you want to play a Demon or Uratha again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T08:56:27-07:00","id":215909,"title":"","content":"Because playing an Unchained or an Uratha means you aren't completely fucked when push comes serious shove. The two combined are potent, and yeah I'd call it as tough as a major template, but it just lacks serious raw power. Both Demons and Werewolves can blow the door down when they need to. A wolf-blooded Heir can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T10:57:11-07:00","id":216015,"title":"","content":"I think it's mixing peas and mashed potatoes. I wouldn't allow it, saying one 'mystical' bloodline overrides the other. But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T12:38:38-07:00","id":216087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/212169-being-a-wolf-blooded-fractal-your-opinion?p=215909#post215909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because playing an Unchained or an Uratha means you aren't completely fucked when push comes serious shove. The two combined are potent, and yeah I'd call it as tough as a major template, but it just lacks serious raw power. Both Demons and Werewolves can blow the door down when they need to. A wolf-blooded Heir can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. A Fractal with the right embeds is easily capable of dishing out damage or taking it just as easily as her Unchained parent. They cannot make pacts or use Exploits ordinarily, and they sure as hell cannot assume a demonic form- but as they can still have access to any manner of embed should they take the time to learn how, they can easily make up for their half breed status. The fact they have a bit more creative freedom what they can do with the powers they have is a boon that doesn't hurt either lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-01-2014, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T10:05:44-07:00","id":218324,"title":"","content":"If I recall, Filamena and Matt have said that it depends on the game in question, but they're even fine with Fractals awakening as Mages, so I would think that Wolf-Blooded probably isn't too far a stretch as long as there's a good in game reason for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T19:25:01-07:00","id":222706,"title":"","content":"So, go check out &quot;The Demon-Blooded Cipher&quot; in HtH.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm fine with Fractal wolf-bloods. And so is the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}